              billion or more as of   September 30, 2016.    The combined assets
              of the  42  large banks totaled    $9.9 trillion, compared to
                 $10.2 trillion for the entire panel of  70  banks, and   $14.1
              trillion for all domestically chartered, federally insured
              commercial banks.
